From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:20:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios/companion: a black band where the interface names no
 background

The renderer fell back to a warm cream (#FFF1C3) when the interface
manifest named no background, which showed as a pale band under a standing
phone's picture. Black is the band's default: the panel's own artwork and
its dock fill carry the colours.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: the companion's band under a standing phone: its interface manifest names no background, so the renderer's default is the band's colour
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the companion
---
 dm/ios/Sources/EdenCompanion.swift | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/ios/Sources/EdenCompanion.swift b/dm/ios/Sources/EdenCompanion.swift
index c80da32a..69250cd6 100644
--- a/dm/ios/Sources/EdenCompanion.swift
+++ b/dm/ios/Sources/EdenCompanion.swift
@@ -827,7 +827,7 @@ private func edenLabelKey(_ text:String,_ scale:Double,_ color:Any?)->String {
                 var nav=context;nav.clip(to:Path(layout.navArt));nav.translateBy(x:layout.navOffset.x,y:layout.navOffset.y);nav.scaleBy(x:layout.navScale,y:layout.navScale);draw(navNodes,f,&nav)
 
             }
-            .background(edenColor(manifest.root["background"],"#FFFFF1C3"))
+            .background(edenColor(manifest.root["background"],"#FF000000"))
             .contentShape(layout.touchShape)
             .gesture(DragGesture(minimumDistance:0).updating($dragTouch){_,active,_ in active=true}.onChanged{g in
                 let inBody=layout.body.contains(g.startLocation)
